An assignment through a parenthesised cast must not load its target.

THE TENTH COPY OF ONE RULE, and the one that kept every wide literal broken.

    *(int*)(p + 4) = 7;      SIGSEGV
    *(int*)p       = 7;      always fine
    x = *(int*)(p + 4);      always fine

So it is the STORE side of the parenthesised-cast path alone. The branch
computed the address, LOADED the int sitting there, and stored through that
value as if it were an address. Experiments entry 17 records this exact line
being fixed for the READ; the store kept its own copy of the rule and never
got the `assigning` guard the other nine paths carry.

WHAT IT COST. tcc writes EVERY WIDE CHARACTER through exactly this shape:

    *(nwchar_t *)(cstr->data + size - sizeof(nwchar_t)) = ch;   tccpp.c:390

so mc-tcc segfaulted on L'a', L'\x1234' and L"abc". tcctest.c's string_test()
is the first function in tcc's own test file to write one, and tcctest.c is the
first thing tcc's test1, test2 and test3 each compile -- so all three died
before producing any output, on a construct 400 lines into a 3,600-line file.

ONLY THE LAST LEVEL IS SPARED. `**(p) = v` still has to load once to reach the
inner pointer. Same rule as zzc, zzg, zzm, zzo and zzzh: an address applies to
the last step of a chain, never to a step that still has to be followed. The
type is stepped either way, because the STORE takes its width from it.

MEASURED. Wide literals compile:

    L'a'   L'\x1234'   L"abc"        rc=0, all three, was SIGSEGV

and tcctest.c advances from line 424 (string_test) to line 1103 (struct_test)
-- 679 lines further into tcc's own test file. It does NOT compile yet; the
next blocker is in struct_test's range and ten probes failed to reproduce it in
isolation, so it is cumulative or not yet spotted. Recorded rather than guessed
at.

PRE-EXISTING, checked directly: the same failure appears on the series with and
without EXPERIMENT-zzzh and zzzi, so this is not fallout from either.

    difftest    92 pass / 0 fail amd64, 94 / 0 aarch64, 1 known gap (case 110)
    the twelve  12 / 12
    tests2      56 of 127 reproduce tcc's own .expect
    corpus      419 / 426
    ladder      libtcc1 7/7, musl idioms 4/4, syscalls run correctly

